00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:11.191
I think having a fugu license
is very important,

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:15.403
and I have one
for Tokyo and Kyoto.

00:03:15.403 --> 00:03:19.324
You can't cook [fugu]
in a restaurant without it.

00:03:19.699 --> 00:03:22.368
Blowfish. Very fatal.

00:03:25.163 --> 00:03:32.003
There are many kinds of fugu.
There are types of fugu skin you can eat

00:03:32.003 --> 00:03:36.507
and others you can't eat, but as a rule,
you can't eat organs.

00:03:36.591 --> 00:03:42.096
If you eat fugu
with a little blood on it,

00:03:42.222 --> 00:03:46.100
it depends on the amount,
but you could even die from it.

00:03:46.184 --> 00:03:48.061
Hence, you need to be really careful.

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:49.103
Basically, there is
no problem if you touch it.

00:03:49.103 --> 00:03:51.147
Basically, there is
no problem if you touch it.

00:03:51.231 --> 00:03:55.401
However, there are public health
regulations that say that

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:57.153
However, there are public health
regulations that say that

00:03:57.278 --> 00:04:02.283
we need to have
a separate cutting board, knife,

00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:04.160
and gloves specifically for fugu.

00:04:04.244 --> 00:04:06.079
This is the guts.

00:04:06.079 --> 00:04:08.081
You have to take off first guts.

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:10.208
Because otherwise, cannot eat.

00:04:10.208 --> 00:04:12.877
The guts inside, I put in a box.

00:04:12.877 --> 00:04:14.963
Then we lock it, hide it.

00:04:14.963 --> 00:04:18.925
The next day, the special
person come to pick up.

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:20.468
This is like, for me,

00:04:20.468 --> 00:04:22.762
it's more fashion.

00:04:22.762 --> 00:04:24.973
It's no realism, unfortunately.

00:04:24.973 --> 00:04:30.645
This preparation is not perfect.

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:33.439
It's 6 out of 10.

00:04:33.564 --> 00:04:35.900
That's very, very dangerous.

00:04:43.866 --> 00:04:45.660
Left-hand side, fish.

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:47.829
Wasabi is this finger.

00:04:47.829 --> 00:04:50.331
Wasabi always put on the fish.

00:04:50.331 --> 00:04:51.541
No put on rice.

00:04:51.541 --> 00:04:54.794
Very soft rice, how do you put on wasabi?

00:04:54.794 --> 00:04:56.421
Because if you put on wasabi,

00:04:56.421 --> 00:04:59.340
it'll be pressure, the rice is broken.

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:00.633
Left-hand side fish,

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:02.427
right-hand side to catch the rice.

00:05:02.427 --> 00:05:05.305
The finger using wasabi, like that.

00:05:07.181 --> 00:05:11.894
It's absolutely essential
to make sushi airy,

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:16.774
so you shouldn't apply too much pressure on it.
It is absolutely essential.

00:05:16.899 --> 00:05:19.319
Over 90% of sushi
restaurants in the world,

00:05:19.319 --> 00:05:20.903
everybody using this.

00:05:20.903 --> 00:05:23.573
But some people using stainless.

00:05:23.573 --> 00:05:25.992
But for me, still, this is the best.

00:05:30.288 --> 00:05:31.414
Some people one finger,

00:05:31.414 --> 00:05:32.874
some people two finger.

00:05:32.874 --> 00:05:34.542
I'm two. Always two finger.

00:05:34.542 --> 00:05:36.878
There are different techniques,

00:05:36.961 --> 00:05:41.257
but what I learned from my master
is the "hontegaeshi" technique,

00:05:41.382 --> 00:05:44.969
which is probably the oldest method.

00:05:44.969 --> 00:05:51.100
It takes five touches
to finish making nigiri sushi.

00:05:51.225 --> 00:05:57.899
My master says it's just the chef's ego
when they say it takes more than five touches.

00:05:58.024 --> 00:06:04.947
Now, why is that?
If you apply fewer touches,

00:06:05.031 --> 00:06:09.160
you will leave fewer fingerprints,

00:06:09.243 --> 00:06:13.539
and your body temperature will not
transfer onto the fish meat.

00:06:13.539 --> 00:06:16.918
That's manga world,
so I can't really

00:06:17.043 --> 00:06:21.839
comment on that.
Anything is ok in a manga.

00:06:21.839 --> 00:06:25.385
It's very difficult for me
to comment on that. 

00:06:25.802 --> 00:06:27.720
Maybe 3, 4, I think.

00:06:34.811 --> 00:06:39.440
It'll be very difficult
to remove bones from

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:46.072
a raw fish. My father, my master,
and I take out

00:06:46.072 --> 00:06:51.869
bones after grilling the fish

00:06:51.869 --> 00:06:56.499
because it makes it easier
to remove them.

00:07:00.586 --> 00:07:02.588
I don't do one knife for everything,

00:07:02.588 --> 00:07:03.881
because no make sense.

00:07:03.881 --> 00:07:05.174
This is deba.

00:07:05.174 --> 00:07:06.676
It only just fillet fish.

00:07:06.676 --> 00:07:10.847
This knife is also using nakiri.

00:07:10.847 --> 00:07:13.891
Nakiri is for using vegetable.

00:07:13.891 --> 00:07:15.393
That's vegetable knife.

00:07:15.393 --> 00:07:18.438
Preparation until service,

00:07:18.438 --> 00:07:20.606
I'm using, like, seven knives.

00:07:20.648 --> 00:07:26.904
Each chef has different ways,
but my master

00:07:26.904 --> 00:07:30.741
taught me to use a different knife
for each ingredient.

00:07:30.825 --> 00:07:34.745
I have a designated knife for tuna,
for white-meat fish,

00:07:34.871 --> 00:07:38.833
and for clams.

00:07:38.875 --> 00:07:41.127
Each fish, I'm changing knife.

00:07:41.127 --> 00:07:43.004
Tuna is more longer.

00:07:43.004 --> 00:07:45.673
A fillet is more thick.

00:07:45.673 --> 00:07:48.968
But to cut sushi is more wider.

00:07:57.310 --> 00:08:00.938
Maybe inside take the brown meat.

00:08:00.938 --> 00:08:03.983
The brown meat is, I
agree, that's amazing.

00:08:03.983 --> 00:08:07.195
I use in my menu spider crab in Cornwall.

00:08:07.195 --> 00:08:09.071
I don't know how to eat the legs.

00:08:09.071 --> 00:08:11.240
Maybe take off the inside meat.

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:16.120
Basically, the shell has
a whole lot of good flavor.

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:20.166
It also has a strong aroma,
so it makes a great broth

00:08:20.249 --> 00:08:25.671
when I stir-fry and then cook it in a dashi broth.

00:08:27.715 --> 00:08:31.135
There are different ways
to do this, so I can't name

00:08:31.427 --> 00:08:36.140
just one. If I hit octopus,

00:08:36.265 --> 00:08:42.396
the cells inside get destroyed,
and then when you cook it,

00:08:42.396 --> 00:08:47.735
since the cells are destroyed,
the octopus is more tender.

00:08:47.818 --> 00:08:52.698
In Spain, for example,
they freeze octopus

00:08:52.782 --> 00:08:58.579
to destroy all the cells,
which is basically the same method.

00:08:58.663 --> 00:09:01.999
In Japan, hitting is
a typical way of doing it

00:09:02.124 --> 00:09:05.878
that has been used for a long time.

00:09:09.048 --> 00:09:13.010
Many guests doesn't like raw
fish, but they want sushi.

00:09:13.010 --> 00:09:14.303
That's a blowtorch.

00:09:14.303 --> 00:09:15.596
It's going to be a little bit grilled.

00:09:15.596 --> 00:09:17.682
It's going to make them more happy to eat.

00:09:17.682 --> 00:09:22.603
But I don't use blowtorches.

00:09:22.687 --> 00:09:28.025
The main reason is
the smell of gas.

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:28.818
Fish meat is very sensitive,
and even that little gas could change

00:09:28.818 --> 00:09:32.905
Fish meat is very sensitive,
and even that little gas could change

00:09:33.030 --> 00:09:36.951
the flavor completely.
I don't recommend it,

00:09:37.034 --> 00:09:43.583
and good sushi restaurants
I know in Tokyo don't use them either.

00:09:47.128 --> 00:09:48.963
It's a great, interesting point,

00:09:48.963 --> 00:09:52.633
because in Japan, after sushi,

00:09:52.633 --> 00:09:54.635
on the top wasabi is never done.

00:09:54.635 --> 00:09:58.180
But always I came to London, since 2006,

00:09:58.180 --> 00:10:00.808
everybody say, "Extra
wasabi, extra wasabi."

00:10:00.808 --> 00:10:02.768
The reason why,

00:10:02.768 --> 00:10:04.562
I don't know how many
passing sushi restaurants

00:10:04.562 --> 00:10:06.188
using fresh wasabi.

00:10:06.188 --> 00:10:08.608
That's why everybody need
more, more, and more.

00:10:08.608 --> 00:10:11.736
Because everybody using
frozen powder wasabi.

00:10:11.736 --> 00:10:15.197
My restaurant using fresh
wasabi I import from Japan.

00:10:15.197 --> 00:10:17.700
That's why aroma, flavor,
it's everything ready.

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:19.035
That's why you don't need extra wasabi.

00:10:19.035 --> 00:10:22.246
Maybe, like, for me, 7 or 8.

00:10:22.246 --> 00:10:25.499
It's very common. It's very basic.

00:10:33.257 --> 00:10:35.843
Yeah, it depends with
the fish how much gram.

00:10:35.843 --> 00:10:40.014
Basically, fish is, like, 8 to 11 gram.

00:10:40.014 --> 00:10:42.433
That's very popular.

00:10:42.433 --> 00:10:43.768
But that's good.

00:10:57.073 --> 00:11:00.701
OK, this way many guests asking me.

00:11:00.701 --> 00:11:02.995
Many sushi chefs

00:11:02.995 --> 00:11:06.165
explain how to eat the sushi.

00:11:06.165 --> 00:11:09.377
Everybody, the fish touch your tongue,

00:11:09.377 --> 00:11:11.170
the rice is up.

00:11:11.170 --> 00:11:13.047
But for me, it no make sense.

00:11:13.047 --> 00:11:15.925
That's why always I explain
to the guests, my guests,

00:11:15.925 --> 00:11:18.010
it's 45 degrees.

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:21.514
No let it touch your tongue first,

00:11:21.514 --> 00:11:22.765
fish directly.

00:11:22.765 --> 00:11:26.769
Because my sushi has a little
bit of salt on the top,

00:11:26.769 --> 00:11:28.437
a little bit citrusy on the top.

00:11:28.437 --> 00:11:30.898
If touches citrus first,
it's completely citrus.

00:11:30.898 --> 00:11:35.277
It's strong, too strong
after biting as well

00:11:35.277 --> 00:11:36.487
to still keep going.

00:11:36.487 --> 00:11:41.492
For me, rice, fish, in
a 45 degree, like that.

00:11:41.826 --> 00:11:45.079
Eat biting two flavors together.

00:11:45.079 --> 00:11:47.581
That's, for me, it more makes sense.

00:11:47.581 --> 00:11:49.166
This my father told me as well.

00:11:49.166 --> 00:11:52.211
For me, it's 9.

00:11:57.007 --> 00:11:59.427
So, they say that he ordered the maguro,

00:11:59.427 --> 00:12:03.764
which is like a sashimi, but random cut.

00:12:07.351 --> 00:12:10.187
First maybe take off the fiber.

00:12:10.187 --> 00:12:13.607
In the front there's a big
fiber in the white one.

00:12:13.607 --> 00:12:18.738
The meat on the corner
of the stomach or the bone

00:12:18.821 --> 00:12:23.033
should be removed with a spoon
since there are no lines in it.

00:12:23.117 --> 00:12:28.038
Hence, when you eat it,
the feeling and taste are refreshing.

00:12:28.164 --> 00:12:32.334
Another way to do it is to cut it
into small pieces,

00:12:32.418 --> 00:12:39.508
but I think scooping out with a spoon
works better for some parts of a fish.

00:12:42.887 --> 00:12:45.431
Using chopsticks is better, yes.

00:12:45.431 --> 00:12:47.558
Because you won't eat --

00:12:47.558 --> 00:12:49.685
it's too much touch to
something like that.

00:12:49.685 --> 00:12:52.897
But also we have very important looks

00:12:52.897 --> 00:12:54.315
in front of the guests.

00:12:54.315 --> 00:12:55.483
Guests are watching us.

00:12:55.483 --> 00:12:56.692
It looks nice.

00:12:56.692 --> 00:12:58.027
Looks more elegant.

00:13:02.281 --> 00:13:03.657
This is one of the ways.

00:13:03.657 --> 00:13:07.745
For me, always, wasabi
on the top of the fish.

00:13:07.745 --> 00:13:09.997
And then soy sauce, and then eat.

00:13:09.997 --> 00:13:11.165
This is my way.

00:13:11.165 --> 00:13:14.043
I just think wasabi, control the wasabi,

00:13:14.043 --> 00:13:15.336
how much put in wasabi,

00:13:15.336 --> 00:13:17.630
also soy sauce, like balance.

00:13:17.630 --> 00:13:19.924
But that one's one other way.

00:13:19.924 --> 00:13:21.383
I'm not complaining.

00:13:21.383 --> 00:13:23.969
Mm, this is very, like, very realistic.

00:13:23.969 --> 00:13:25.179
Maybe 10 out of 10.

00:13:25.179 --> 00:13:26.347
This is very real.

00:13:26.347 --> 00:13:28.557
Chef: Eight parts rice
vinegar, four parts sugar,

00:13:28.557 --> 00:13:29.850
one part sea salt.

00:13:29.850 --> 00:13:32.269
Eight, four, one, OK?

00:13:32.269 --> 00:13:34.605
Stirring sushi rice is —

00:13:34.688 --> 00:13:39.693
Rice makes up 80% of sushi,

00:13:39.819 --> 00:13:42.863
so it's a very important ingredient
in sushi.

00:13:43.113 --> 00:13:49.662
Mixing rice vinegar is

00:13:49.745 --> 00:13:54.625
a very sensitive process. Hence,
I have to try not to touch

00:13:54.708 --> 00:13:59.755
the rice a lot and add vinegar
while blowing air on the rice.

00:13:59.839 --> 00:14:06.512
To do that, I should stir
as little as possible.

00:14:06.637 --> 00:14:09.306
Chef: Cut the rice at a 45-degree angle.

00:14:09.306 --> 00:14:13.060
Mix them thoroughly so that
every grain of rice is seasoned.

00:14:13.060 --> 00:14:15.938
Mm, that's true.

00:14:15.938 --> 00:14:18.524
Maybe more angle, I
think. Little bit more.

00:14:18.524 --> 00:14:22.987
I teach my pupils to make a rice 
paddle as flat as possible

00:14:23.112 --> 00:14:26.448
and reduce the number of times
they touch the rice.

00:14:26.574 --> 00:14:30.536
For me, if my staff do the same way,

00:14:30.536 --> 00:14:32.663
maybe I bring to the bat.

00:14:32.663 --> 00:14:33.998
Something like that.

00:14:33.998 --> 00:14:36.125
Yes.
[crew laughing]

00:14:36.125 --> 00:14:37.251
I'm not hitting, but

00:14:37.251 --> 00:14:39.795
I just give pressure.
[crew laughing]

00:14:39.795 --> 00:14:41.505
Yes.
[crew laughing]

00:14:41.505 --> 00:14:45.926
I'm slicing this like the sushi chefs do.

00:14:45.926 --> 00:14:47.970
They cut against the grain.

00:14:48.012 --> 00:14:52.141
It would be a different story

00:14:52.141 --> 00:14:57.229
if she had a reason to cut a line like that, but it looked 
like she was  just cutting it like that for no reason.

00:14:57.354 --> 00:15:00.149
The lines can differ depending
on the type of fish

00:15:00.190 --> 00:15:02.943
and the part of the fish. If you
don't know that while cutting,

00:15:03.068 --> 00:15:09.533
customers will not like
the texture of the fish.

00:15:15.623 --> 00:15:18.542
I really recommend, if you make sushi,

00:15:18.542 --> 00:15:20.711
have your hands cold.

00:15:20.711 --> 00:15:24.965
Maybe very cold water, soak a little bit,

00:15:24.965 --> 00:15:27.509
like, 20 seconds, 30 seconds.

00:15:27.509 --> 00:15:28.719
It's got to be cold.

00:15:28.719 --> 00:15:29.762
That's maybe better.

00:15:29.762 --> 00:15:31.805
And also before touch rice,

00:15:31.805 --> 00:15:33.599
little bit water,

00:15:33.599 --> 00:15:36.477
wet hand, then touching better.

00:15:36.477 --> 00:15:38.979
This is like, for me, very true

00:15:38.979 --> 00:15:40.439
because this is beginner.

00:15:40.439 --> 00:15:41.857
That's why maybe 7.

00:15:47.738 --> 00:15:49.490
That's quite interesting,

00:15:49.490 --> 00:15:52.534
because my restaurant is omakase.

00:15:52.534 --> 00:15:54.036
It's 20 courses.

00:15:54.036 --> 00:15:58.999
And then between sushi is small
kind of bite and hot food.

00:15:58.999 --> 00:16:01.669
Because too much rice is quite full.

00:16:01.669 --> 00:16:04.755
